1
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:39,333
When it happens... there's nothing like it!

2
00:11:06,666 --> 00:11:12,666
Sunshine on Leith is a music, comedy, drama film directed by Dexter Fletcher.

3
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:46,000
Davy and Ally have to re-learn how to live life in Edinburgh
after coming home from serving in Afghanistan.

4
00:22:13,333 --> 00:22:19,333
Both struggle to learn to live a life outside the army and to deal with
the everyday struggles of family, jobs and relationships.

5
00:27:46,666 --> 00:27:52,666
Sunshine on Leith is based on the sensational stage hit of the same
name, featuring music by pop-folk band The Proclaimers.

6
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Davy Henshaw, played by George MacKay.

7
00:38:53,333 --> 00:38:59,333
Ally, played by Kevin Guthrie.

8
00:44:26,666 --> 00:44:32,666
Ronnie, played by Paul Brannigan.

9
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Jean Henshaw, played by Jane Horrocks.

10
00:55:33,333 --> 00:55:39,333
Robert 'Rab' Henshaw, played by Peter Mullan.

11
01:01:06,666 --> 01:01:12,666
Liz Henshaw, played by Freya Mavor.

12
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
Sunshine on Leith is a 2013 Scottish romantic
musical film directed by Dexter Fletcher.

13
01:12:13,333 --> 01:12:19,333
It is an adaptation of the stage musical of the same name, a
jukebox musical featuring songs by the Proclaimers.

14
01:17:46,666 --> 01:17:52,666
It was screened in the Special Presentation section at the
2013 Toronto International Film Festival.

15
01:23:20,000 --> 01:23:26,000
The songs, arranged by musical director Paul
Englishby, are performed by the cast.

16
01:28:53,333 --> 01:28:59,333
The Proclaimers themselves appear in a brief cameo.

17
01:34:26,666 --> 01:34:32,666
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
